Description
We are seeking a seasoned Java Developer with experience in Java/J2EE, Spring Boot, microservices and distributed systems to develop and support Cash Management applications in a banking environment.<br/><br/>Mandatory Skill(s)
Must have 7–9 years of hands-on Java/J2EE development experience;
Must have strong Java, Spring Boot, Spring Integration and microservices expertise;
Experience with Kafka, Spark and Flink;
Hands-on Docker, Kubernetes and CI/CD tools;
Strong TDD/BDD experience with JUnit, Mockito and Cucumber;
Good knowledge of architecture, design patterns and performance tuning;
Strong Agile/Scrum and stakeholder management experience;<br/><br/>Desirable Skill(s)
Experience with Elasticsearch, HBase, HDFS and MongoDB;
Basic cash management or banking domain knowledge;
Financial industry experience;
Experience in solution design, UML and application migrations;
Experience mentoring developers and supporting technical leads;<br/><br/>Responsibilities
Develop and enhance Cash Management and reporting applications;
Maintain application stability, performance and support;
Lead solution design, estimation and implementation of new features;
Develop quality solutions using TDD/BDD practices;
Collaborate with Product Owners, BAs and business stakeholders;
Support Agile delivery and cross-functional project teams;
Troubleshoot issues and drive technical improvements;
Mentor junior developers and support the Technical Lead;<br/><br/>Should you be interested in this career opportunity, please send in your updated resume to<br/><br/>(HIDDEN TEXT)<br/><br/>at the earliest.<br/><br/>When you apply, you voluntarily consent to the disclosure, collection and use of your personal data for employment/recruitment and related purposes in accordance with the SCIENTE Group Privacy Policy, a copy of which is published at SCIENTE&#39;s website (https://www.sciente.com/privacy-policy).<br/><br/>Confidentiality is assured, and only shortlisted candidates will be notified for interviews.<br/><br/>EA Licence No. 07C5639
